# C3: the std submodules mlmf-safetensors may name. Started EMPTY at the
# crate skeleton and grows one commit at a time; the first three entries
# landed with task 1, the header stage, which is the first code here.
#
# A permission granted before its use is a permission nobody re-examines.
# mlmf-gguf started this file empty too and grew it one commit at a time,
# each entry landing beside the code that forced it. Add an entry only in
# the commit that needs it, and say in a comment what forced it.

# Task 1, the header stage. Each entry names what forced it.
#
# `error` -- `impl std::error::Error for SafetensorsError`. The trait lives
#   in std and there is no other way to spell it; this crate does not depend
#   on `thiserror`.
# `fmt` -- the `Display` impls on `Stage` and `SafetensorsError`, which are
#   what make the error printable at a consumer's edge.
# `str` -- `std::str::from_utf8` on the header bytes, so that "not UTF-8" is
#   its own error kind rather than serde's guess at a syntax error. Spelled
#   with the `std::` prefix on purpose: the bare `str::from_utf8` associated
#   function reaches the same code and is invisible to this allow-list, and a
#   gate that can be stepped around by dropping four characters is not one.
error
fmt
str
